decision: changes-requested

Both prior findings are fixed. Two medium blockers remain:

- **N3 — Windows test compilation:** [review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go:463](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1993394050/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go:463) calls `syscall.Mkfifo` without a build constraint. Windows has no such symbol; the runtime skip cannot prevent compilation failure.
- **N4 — First-open FIFO race:** [review_adapter_containment.go:626](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1993394050/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go:626) can block indefinitely if a FIFO replaces the directory between `Lstat` and `OpenRoot`. The regression covers a later window.

Targeted Linux tests passed. Artifact and surface checks passed; artifact-check reported 955 warnings and no blocking findings. Windows test cross-compilation was blocked by the read-only filesystem; target-aware source selection and symbol inspection establish N3. No repository changes or attestation were made.

Applied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules.

